& =\frac{\ln{z}}{\ln{w}} \\
& =\frac{\ln{\left\vert z \right\vert}+i(\arg{z}+2\pi n)}{\ln{\left\vert w \right\vert}+i(\arg{w}+2\pi n)} ,n \in \mathbb{Z} \\
& =\frac{\ln{\left\vert z \right\vert}+i\arg{z}}{\ln{\left\vert w \right\vert}+i\arg{w}}
\end{align}

